profiles = [
 {"chainId": 999, "lens": "L1",
  "summary": "Twenty two opcode and call probes gave the same words, including the gas figures, on the official node, on the archive client and on the testnet node. The archive client now carries a second spec id for the fork of 2026-11-11 and both ids still map to Cancun. The testnet shows no sign of a later EVM fork.",
  "deltas": [
   {"delta": "One eth_call with two stub contracts placed by state override ran 22 steps on the official node (client string hyperliquid evm Mainnet), on the archive client and on the testnet node. A TSTORE made in a call that then ends in REVERT, in INVALID or out of gas reads back as 0. A TSTORE made in a successful inner call is gone when the frame above it reverts. TSTORE under STATICCALL fails and TLOAD under STATICCALL works. A value stored in one call is read in a later call of the same execution. DELEGATECALL writes the caller's transient slot. A call that forwards all gas left the callee 1,694,214 of 1,721,406 gas on all three nodes. A value call to an address without code succeeds with no return data and moves the value. A value call above the balance fails and the caller continues. A value call with gas 0 gave the callee 2,154 gas after its own dispatch, which is the 2,300 stipend. MCOPY and PUSH0 work. All 65 result words are equal on the three nodes.",
    "source": OFF + " , " + ARCH + " and " + TEST + " eth_call with state override on 2026-11-23; script cycles/007/hyperevm.work/opprobe.py, results raw/opprobe_official_archive.json and raw/opprobe_testnet.json", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The archive client defines HlSpecId V2, described as MRB precompile accounting and Osaka ModExp, active from mainnet block 50,988,232 and testnet block 69,259,950. V1 and V2 both convert to revm SpecId CANCUN. V2 replaces the ModExp precompile at 0x05 with revm's Osaka version and multiplies the gas of ecrecover by 5, of ModExp, the three bn254 precompiles and blake2f by 10, and of the KZG precompile by 40. The instruction table is revm's mainnet table with one replacement, BLOCKHASH below block 243,538. Bybit's notice names the same height and the date 2026-11-11 for the upgrade it calls nb-20261110.",
    "source": NR + "src/evm/spec.rs lines 5 to 19, " + NR + "src/node/evm/mrb.rs lines 10 to 13 and 64 to 79, " + NR + "src/node/evm/factory.rs lines 79 to 138, " + NR + "src/evm/api/mod.rs lines 33 to 43, https://announcements.bybit.com/en/article/bybit-to-support-hyperevm-hype-nb-20261110-network-upgrade--art7a2162c994b9/", "relevance": "none"},
   {"delta": "Upcoming forks. The testnet node (chain 998, block 70,407,986) answers 584 low and special addresses in the same classes as mainnet. The read precompiles end at 0x0814 on both, 0x0b to 0x11 and 0x0100 are silent on both, and neither block header has a requestsHash field. The two differences are ordinary contracts that someone deployed on testnet at the EIP-2935 and EIP-4788 addresses (83 and 97 bytes). The docs still state Cancun without blobs. I found no announcement of Prague, EIP-7702 or a gas limit change for HyperEVM. One vendor wrote in October 2025 that it will add EIP-7702 relaying once HyperEVM supports it.",
    "source": TEST + " and " + OFF + " eth_call, eth_getCode and eth_getBlockByNumber on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/lowaddr.py, raw/lowaddr_main_vs_test.json); " + DOCS + "for-developers/hyperevm.md; https://blog.thirdweb.com/changelog/account-abstraction-now-available-on-hyperliquid/", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "In the revm revision that the archive client pins, a call frame looks up a precompile by the address whose code is run (bytecode_address). A DELEGATECALL frame carries the caller of the frame above it and that frame's value as an apparent value with no transfer, and a CALLCODE frame transfers from the calling contract to itself. A precompile reached by DELEGATECALL from a contract that the PoolManager called is therefore handed the PoolManager as caller and the payout amount as value. Balance moves only when the value is of the Transfer kind.",
    "source": RV + "crates/handler/src/frame.rs lines 166 to 201, " + RV + "crates/interpreter/src/instructions/contract.rs lines 158 to 163, 216 to 221, 267 to 272 and 316 to 321", "relevance": "low"}
  ]},
 {"chainId": 999, "lens": "L2",
  "summary": "The gas of a sendToEvmWithData call is now capped at 200,000 by the node, and 3,179 system transactions in the newest 4,000 blocks all sit ahead of the signed ones with 200,000 gas, or 30,000 for HYPE credits. The testnet has the same pair of unsigned senders as mainnet for USDC, and one of them is a contract. The deployed PoolManager, called through a stub on the official node, enforces the lock, the delta count and the native value guard as src/ states.",
  "deltas": [
   {"delta": "The Hyperliquid API announcements channel stated on 2026-11-19 that from the next network upgrade sendToEvmWithData consumes at most 200k gas even if a higher gas limit is passed. The next upgrade was announced for about 09:30 UTC on 2026-11-21. The dates are from a channel mirror that shows local time, and I matched its offset to UTC on one post only. The wording implies that a higher limit took effect before that upgrade.",
    "source": TG + " (posts dated 19 Nov and 20 Nov 2026), https://tg.me/hyperliquid_api/387 for the time offset", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Census of blocks 52,048,026 to 52,052,025 on the archive endpoint: 3,179 transactions with gas price 0, none placed after a signed transaction. 1,144 are USDC transfer calls sent in the name of the CoreDepositWallet contract 0x6b9e773128f453f5c2c60935ee2de2cbc5390a24, 673 are USDC transfer calls sent in the name of the treasury address 0xc20699185c15d0a2fd65779bb5d69f5b0b113c00, 1,004 are transfer calls from 0x20 system addresses to 36 linked contracts, 336 are coreReceiveWithData calls (selector 0x6ddde35e) on the CoreDepositWallet, and 22 are HYPE credits from 0x2222222222222222222222222222222222222222. Every call to a contract carries 200,000 gas and every HYPE credit 30,000. No system transaction names the PoolManager as sender or target.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_getBlockByNumber with full transactions for 4,000 blocks on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/systx.py, raw/systx_census.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The block data that the validator node publishes now gives a sender for each system transaction. The archive client's SystemTx type has an optional from field and prefers it over every derived sender. A code comment calls it the authoritative upstream from. Before the field existed the client recovered the sender of testnet USDC system transactions from the Transfer log, for testnet blocks 55,231,857 to 55,432,000. The official replay client on its main branch has no such field: its SystemTx holds tx and receipt only, and it takes the sender from the target contract through a map of linked contracts, or uses the HYPE bridge address when the input is empty. It asserts that its receipt equals the recorded one.",
    "source": NR + "src/node/types/mod.rs lines 215 to 221, " + NR + "src/node/types/reth_compat.rs lines 183 to 207, " + NR + "src/node/types/patch.rs lines 11 to 21, " + SY + "src/types.rs lines 53 to 56, " + SY + "src/run.rs lines 217 to 238", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The testnet repeats the mainnet AQAv2 pattern for USDC. The testnet USDC token is 0x2b3370ee501b4a559b57d449569354196457d8ab and HyperCore links it to 0x0b80659a4076e9e93c7dbe0f10675a16a3e5c206, a contract of 2,175 bytes whose account nonce is 28,681. A contract's nonce rises only when it creates contracts or when transactions are sent in its name, and the testnet node lists a system transaction with this contract in the from field (block 55,432,087, nonce 183, gas 200,000, no signature). The second sender, 0xf9b10ef826e9aa275f1813034e3bd9b80224e535, has no code, nonce 12,405 and exactly 1.0 HYPE. The HyperCore explorer shows two actions signed by that address on 2026-06-05, so on testnet the second sender has an owner who signs for it.",
    "source": TEST + " eth_getCode, eth_getTransactionCount, eth_getBalance and eth_getSystemTxsByBlockNumber for blocks 0x34ac571 and 0x34dd397; https://api.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/info spotMeta; https://rpc.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/explorer userDetails; queried 2026-11-23", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The HyperCore explorer lists 13 actions for Coinbase's staking account 0x4E5319dEb1072B01439EE674db5C321d11fd96F8. One is authorizeAqav2Role with token 0 and role treasury, in HyperCore block 1,020,511,746 on 2026-06-02 21:16:15 UTC. The action has no address field and none of the other 12 actions names the treasury address. The explorer lists no action at all for the treasury address 0xc20699185c15D0a2fD65779BB5d69f5b0B113c00. The place where HyperCore records the treasury address is therefore outside the deployer's documented action, in a validator vote or in an action that the public docs and the Python SDK do not describe.",
    "source": "https://rpc.hyperliquid.xyz/explorer userDetails for both addresses on 2026-11-23 (raw/explorer_main_0x4E5319dE.json); " + DOCS + "for-developers/api/exchange-endpoint.md; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hyperliquid-dex/hyperliquid-python-sdk/master/hyperliquid/exchange.py", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Behaviour of the deployed PoolManager on the official node, tested by eth_call through a caller stub placed by state override. A take of 1 wei followed by settle with value 1 closes the unlock. The same pair after sync(WHYPE) reverts with NonzeroNativeValue. Adding sync(address(0)) before the settle makes it pass again. A take left unpaid reverts with CurrencyNotSettled. settle outside unlock reverts with ManagerLocked. The archive endpoint gives the same six answers.",
    "source": OFF + " and " + ARCH + " eth_call with state override on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/pmbehave.py, raw/pm_behaviour.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "All 2,760 transactions that emitted a PoolManager log since block 45,998,366 were traced. None ends with a token sync that no settle consumed. 85 make a native settle without a sync of their own and 55 of those are not the first transaction of their block. In those 55 blocks an earlier transaction called the PoolManager in 6 cases and none of them left a sync behind.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_getLogs, debug_traceTransaction and debug_traceBlockByNumber with callTracer on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/l415.py and l415b.py, raw/l415b.json)", "relevance": "low"}
  ]},
 {"chainId": 999, "lens": "L3",
  "summary": "The PoolManager holds a nonzero balance of 262 of its 307 ERC-20 pool currencies. Fourteen groups of equal balances hold 144 tokens, and in no group does a transfer of one token move the balance of another. Nine tokens of one launch product refuse every plain transfer from the PoolManager. The notice that USDC sent to HyperCore below 1 USDC is not credited adds a case to the known stranded payout family.",
  "deltas": [
   {"delta": "Equal balance grouping at block 52,051,531: balanceOf(PoolManager) for the 307 ERC-20 currencies of the 344 pools gives 262 nonzero balances and 14 groups of identical nonzero balances with 144 members (sizes 68, 35, 9, 8, 4, 3, 3 and seven pairs). The large groups are launch tokens with the same supply and the same first swap. For each member a stub at the PoolManager address sent one unit and then read all balances of the group. In 135 tests only the token's own balance fell, by exactly one unit. In 9 tests the transfer reverted.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_getLogs for the Initialize topic, eth_call balanceOf and eth_call with state override on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/pools.py and equalbal.py, raw/equalbal.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The 9 tokens that revert are PIPFSTR, ODDSTR, SLIMESTR, WHAL3SSTR, HYPIOSTR, THCSTR, HFAXSTR, HYPURRSTR and REKTSTR, each a 121 byte proxy with the PoolManager address in its immutable data. Each is paired with native HYPE in one pool under the verified hook NFTStrategyHook at 0x317e01adf67b95a2d817c279b9f78d758fbc2444 or 0xea456a0bf66a888cd1c614516496d02608cf2444. The PoolManager holds 999,999,999.999999999999994637 of each. A transfer of one unit from the PoolManager to a codeless address, to an ordinary account and to the PositionManager reverts with selector 0x2f352531, which is InvalidTransfer(). For HYPURRSTR a transfer to its hook reverts in the same way. Eight of the nine pools have no swap and one has three. I did not read the token implementation, so the condition under which the token allows the transfer is not established.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_call and eth_getCode on 2026-11-23; https://sourcify.dev/server/v2/contract/999/0x317e01adf67b95a2d817c279b9f78d758fbc2444?fields=sources", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "The API announcements channel stated on 2026-11-07 that USDC transfers from HyperEVM to HyperCore have a 1 USDC minimum and that smaller amounts are not credited on HyperCore. A payout of less than 1 USDC to the USDC path into HyperCore now leaves the EVM balance and credits nobody, where before it was credited to the sender's HyperCore account.",
    "source": TG + " (post dated 07 Nov 2026)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Position 123 of the pool 0xa2892acf47d712888c3d619ef245feb569c1973feb1d1ef5b36c1866eddbe3e7 has the range -12600 to 887220 and at block 52,026,657 the pool price was sqrtPriceX96 42197598878763279489260510356 at tick -12600, the lower bound of the range. The position was owed 0 of currency1 0x883dad2aa97175c0d1569e1de61204ac47b2b8fb in principal and in fees, and the PoolManager held 0 of that token.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_call to StateView 0x1656326235cb9E34Cb58CaDe53AE30789AB32A1A (getSlot0, getPositionInfo, getFeeGrowthInside) at block 52,026,657", "relevance": "none"}
  ]},
 {"chainId": 999, "lens": "L4",
  "summary": "No precompile or system contract acts on the account of an inherited caller. The 21 read precompiles return the same bytes under CALL, STATICCALL, DELEGATECALL and CALLCODE and never use the caller or the value. The bridge and CoreWriter are bytecode, so a delegated call emits their log from the calling contract, and chain history shows that HyperCore ignored such a log.",
  "deltas": [
   {"delta": "Read precompile sweep from an inner frame. A forwarding stub at the PoolManager address called a second stub with 0.001 HYPE, and the second stub called each address from 0x0800 to 0x082f with eleven input shapes. 0x0800 to 0x0814 are precompiles and 0x0815 to 0x082f answer like accounts without code. 0x0803, 0x0804, 0x0805 and 0x0810 accept any input of 32 or 64 bytes, 0x0809 accepts every input, and the others accept only inputs whose first word fits their argument. Earlier sweeps used empty input and recorded twenty of them only as failing.",
    "source": OFF + " eth_call with state override on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/sweep_read.py, raw/read_sweep_call_main.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Each of the 21 read precompiles was then called with CALL, CALL with 7 wei, STATICCALL, DELEGATECALL, CALLCODE and CALLCODE with 7 wei, for inputs that succeed and one that fails. The success flag and the return bytes are the same for all six kinds. The one exception is 0x0809, whose value follows the latest HyperCore block between two requests. CALL with value leaves the 7 wei at the precompile address when the call succeeds and returns it when the call fails. DELEGATECALL and CALLCODE move no balance. The standard precompiles 0x01 to 0x0a behave the same way. Five precompile addresses already hold HYPE that earlier callers left there: 0x01 holds 0.227, 0x02 holds 0.131, 0x03 holds 1.10, 0x0807 holds 0.01 and 0x080a holds 1.0.",
    "source": OFF + " eth_call with state override on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/kinds_read.py, raw/read_kinds_main.json and raw/std_and_system_kinds.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "In the archive client a read precompile is a closure that looks up the pair of input bytes and gas limit in the results recorded with the block. It reads input.data and input.gas and no other field of the call, so the caller, the value and the call kind cannot change the answer.",
    "source": NR + "src/node/evm/executor.rs lines 66 to 87 and 304 to 323", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Traces with logs on the archive client: DELEGATECALL into the code of 0x2222222222222222222222222222222222222222 from a contract that the PoolManager called with 0.001 HYPE emits Received with the PoolManager as user and 0.001 HYPE as amount, and the emitting address is the calling contract. CALLCODE emits it with the calling contract as user. CoreWriter reverts under DELEGATECALL when the frame carries value and under any call with value. From a frame without value, CALLCODE into CoreWriter emits RawAction with the calling contract as user, and DELEGATECALL emits it with the PoolManager as user and a spot send payload. In every case the log comes from an address other than the system contract.",
    "source": ARCH + " debug_traceCall with callTracer, withLog and state overrides on 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/trace_sys.py, raw/trace_sys_contracts.json and raw/trace_delegate_zero_value.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "Of 859,223 logs with the topic of Received(address,uint256) in the whole chain history, 18,329 come from 1,225 emitters other than the bridge address, and 11,613 of those have the same layout as the bridge log. In block 49,185,997 (2026-10-22 02:32:22 UTC) the contract 0xd4cbc0953d9e291a55e590f0acc1de0c3d05f3f7 emitted Received for user 0xd377621a703210ca2b547bc9df51c539c1c9fa68 and 0.0001 HYPE without paying the bridge. The same user had made a real bridge payment of 0.0001 HYPE 226 seconds earlier in block 49,185,767. The HyperCore ledger of that user shows one credit of 0.0001 HYPE from the bridge address, at the second of the real payment, and no other entry within one hour on either side. Thirteen further samples from other emitters show no credit either.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_getLogs in 50,000 block windows, eth_getTransactionReceipt and debug_traceTransaction; https://api.hyperliquid.xyz/info userNonFundingLedgerUpdates; queried 2026-11-23 (cycles/007/hyperevm.work/forged_logs.py, raw/forged_logs.json.gz and raw/forged_received_core_check.json)", "relevance": "low"},
   {"delta": "In the last 600,000 blocks 76,902 logs carry the RawAction topic and 12 come from two other emitters. One is a 79 byte contract that on 2026-11-18 emitted the topic with the user 0xf036a5261406a394bd63eb4df49c464634a66155, an account with 867,470 USDC on HyperCore, and 164 zero bytes of data. The other, 0x7246bc27cdf93e273822a1380a3b080940e31bbb, copies the CoreWriter interface for a product of its own and emitted eleven well formed spot send actions of 5,000 USDC in the name of contracts that have no HyperCore account. HyperCore shows no ledger entry for any of the named users or for the destination. Neither case is a clean test, because the first payload is no action and the second set of senders holds nothing on HyperCore.",
    "source": ARCH + " eth_getLogs, eth_getCode; https://api.hyperliquid.xyz/info userNonFundingLedgerUpdates, userRole and spotClearinghouseState; queried 2026-11-23 (raw/forged_rawaction_core_check.json)", "relevance": "low"}
  ]}
]

findings = [
 {"ref": "F-020",
  "title": "HyperCore sends unsigned transfers in the name of addresses that never signed, including a contract, and the record that names such an address is outside the deployer's documented action",
  "chainIds": [999], "lens": "L2", "assumptions": ["A2", "A8"], "effect": "siphon", "actor": "operator", "severity": "medium",
  "difference": "HyperCore places system transactions at the top of HyperEVM blocks. They carry no signature and gas price 0, and the node states the sender. Under AQAv2 the node sends token transfers in the name of the token's linked contract and of a treasury address, to hold their balances in a ratio of 1 to 9. The published block data gives a from field for each such transaction and the archive client takes the sender from that field. On Ethereum a balance leaves an address only through a transaction that the address signed or a call made by its own code.",
  "mechanism": "1. What is new in this cycle. The treasury deployer's own action cannot be the place where the treasury address is named. The HyperCore explorer lists 13 actions for Coinbase's staking account. Its AQAv2 action is authorizeAqav2Role with the fields token 0 and role treasury, sent on 2026-06-02, and none of the 13 actions contains the address 0xc20699185c15D0a2fD65779BB5d69f5b0B113c00. The explorer lists no action for that address. The address was therefore recorded by a validator vote or by an action that the public docs and SDK do not describe. 2. The testnet shows the same mechanism with a contract as sender. Testnet USDC is linked to 0x0b80659a4076e9e93c7dbe0f10675a16a3e5c206, which has 2,175 bytes of code and an account nonce of 28,681, and the testnet node lists a system transaction with that contract in the from field. A contract cannot sign, so the node alone produced those 28,681 transactions. 3. On mainnet the newest 4,000 blocks hold 1,144 transfers sent in the name of the CoreDepositWallet contract and 673 in the name of the treasury address, all with 200,000 gas and all ahead of the signed transactions. 4. The archive client sets disable_eip3607 for every transaction, which is what lets a sender with code pass, and it treats the upstream from field as authoritative. The official replay client has no such field. 5. If HyperCore recorded the PoolManager as the treasury address of a token, or as the address a later rule of this kind names, the node would send transfer calls on that token with the PoolManager as msg.sender. The token would move the balance. Nothing in src compares pool accounting with a token balance outside the window between sync and settle (src/PoolManager.sol:279-288 and 349-365), so pools and claims would still record the tokens as owed and later takes would revert in the token transfer (src/types/Currency.sol:55-87). 6. Still unknown: which HyperCore record names the treasury address, whether the node tests that address in any way, and whether it can be changed after activation. The validator node is closed source. AQAv2 is announced as a requirement for quote assets of HIP-4 and validator-operated perp markets in a future network upgrade, so more tokens are likely to get such a record.",
  "impact": "All pools and ERC-6909 claims in a token for which HyperCore recorded the PoolManager as the address to rebalance from. USDC is the one AQAv2 token today, its treasury address is Coinbase's, and no system transaction in the samples of this and earlier cycles names the PoolManager. An ordinary account cannot bring this about.",
  "preconditions": "A validator vote, or whatever privileged record names a treasury address, must name the PoolManager. The deployers must each stake 500,000 HYPE. The linked contract's balance must sit below its tenth for transfers to flow out of the named address.",
  "mitigations": "Ask the Hyperliquid team which record names an AQAv2 treasury address and whether the node refuses an address with code. Watch eth_getSystemTxsByBlockNumber, or the from field of the published block data, for a system transaction whose sender is the PoolManager. Treat every AQAv2 quote token as depending on the validator set in this respect.",
  "coreRefs": ["src/PoolManager.sol:279-288", "src/PoolManager.sol:349-365", "src/types/Currency.sol:55-87"],
  "sources": [
   {"url": "https://rpc.hyperliquid.xyz/explorer userDetails for 0x4E5319dEb1072B01439EE674db5C321d11fd96F8 and 0xc20699185c15D0a2fD65779BB5d69f5b0B113c00, queried 2026-11-23", "supports": "13 actions of the staking account, one authorizeAqav2Role with token 0 and role treasury on 2026-06-02 and none that contains the treasury address; no action for the treasury address"},
   {"url": TEST + " eth_getCode, eth_getTransactionCount and eth_getSystemTxsByBlockNumber 0x34dd397; https://api.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/info spotMeta", "supports": "Testnet USDC is linked to a contract of 2,175 bytes with nonce 28,681 that appears as the from address of an unsigned system transaction"},
   {"url": ARCH + " eth_getBlockByNumber for blocks 52,048,026 to 52,052,025", "supports": "1,144 system transfers in the name of the CoreDepositWallet contract and 673 in the name of the treasury address, 200,000 gas each, none after a signed transaction, none naming the PoolManager"},
   {"url": NR + "src/node/types/reth_compat.rs", "supports": "Lines 183 to 207: the sender of a system transaction is taken from the upstream from field when present"},
   {"url": NR + "src/node/evm/config.rs", "supports": "Lines 329 to 331: disable_eip3607 is set for every transaction, so a sender with code is accepted"},
   {"url": SY + "src/run.rs", "supports": "Lines 217 to 238: the official replay client derives the sender from the target contract and has no from field"},
   {"url": DOCS + "hypercore/aligned-quote-assets.md", "supports": "The treasury deployer designates a treasury address, activation is by validator vote, balances are held 9 to 1, and AQAv2 will be required for quote assets of HIP-4 and validator-operated perp markets"},
   {"url": DOCS + "for-developers/api/exchange-endpoint.md", "supports": "authorizeAqav2Role has the fields token and role and no address"}
  ],
  "evidence": "primary"}
]

